Template: tapir/adopt
Type: boolean
Default: true
Description: Move the existing Tapir installation into containers?
 A Tapir installation of an earlier version of this package was found
 (/etc/tapir/tapir.env). It becomes the container instance below with the
 same database, files and port; Keycloak moves to the shared container unless
 the configured one is reachable.

Template: tapir/create_instance
Type: boolean
Default: true
Description: Create a Tapir instance now?
 Further instances (one per solidarity farm) are created later with
 "tapir-instance create".

Template: tapir/instance_name
Type: string
Default: tapir
Description: Name of the instance:
 Short name, also the Keycloak realm: a-z, 0-9 and -, e.g. ackervielfalt.

Template: tapir/domain
Type: string
Default:
Description: Public host name of the instance:
 E.g. tapir.example.org. The nginx site, the Keycloak realm and all URLs are
 derived from it.

Template: tapir/port
Type: string
Default: 8000
Description: Local port of the instance:
 gunicorn listens on 127.0.0.1:<port>, redis on <port> + 10000.

Template: tapir/admin_email
Type: string
Default:
Description: E-mail address of the first admin:
 Gets a Tapir account with a Keycloak login; the initial password is written
 to /etc/tapir/initial-passwords/. Leave empty to skip.

Template: tapir/image
Type: string
Default: ghcr.io/beerlesklopfer/wirgarten-tapir:latest
Description: Container image of Tapir:
